{"id":3828,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/whose-possessive-s/","parentId":540,"order":75,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Whose, possessive ‘s: Whose is this? It’s Mike’s","seo":{"title":"Whose, possessive 's: Whose is this? It's Mike's - Test-English","description":"Learn to use possessive 's and 'whose' in English with simple explanations and engaging exercises in this A1 elementary grammar lesson.","image":"/media/uploads/A1%E2%80%93Grammar_Possessive-s_Whose-1.png"},"modified":"2025-05-13T08:19:37","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct option to complete the sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"438\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct forms:&nbsp;<em>whose,&nbsp;who’s</em> possessive ‘s, etc.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"439\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Rewrite the sentences using the possessive <strong>‘s</strong> as in the example.</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: The box belongs to Jane. ⇒ It’s <span class=\"textGap\">Jane’s box</span>.</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"440\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<h3>Possessive <strong>‘s</strong>: Use and form</h3> <p><img src=\"/media/uploads/possessive-s-use-form.png\" alt=\"Informative grammar chart explaining the use and form of possessive 's in English, with rules for singular, plural, and irregular nouns, and examples.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-18610\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h3>Possessive <strong>‘s</strong>: Use</h3> <p>We use&nbsp;<strong>‘s</strong> to show that something belongs to a person (or a pet) or to talk about relationships between people.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>This is Peter<span><strong>‘s father</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>This is <strong><span>the father of</span></strong> Peter.<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>Peter and Mary<span><strong>‘s</strong></span> car is red.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>My cat<span><strong>‘s</strong></span> ears are white.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>We also use the possessive&nbsp;<strong>‘s&nbsp;</strong>to talk about shops and houses.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I am at John<strong><span>‘s</span></strong>.</em> (= at John’s house)</li> <li><em>I need to go to the chemist<strong><span>‘s</span></strong>.&nbsp;</em>(= the chemist’s shop)</li> </ul> <h3>Possessive <strong>‘s</strong>: Form</h3> <p>Singular noun + <strong>‘s</strong></p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Anna’s</strong></span> clothes, <span><strong>Chris’s</strong></span> wife, the <span><strong>student’s</strong></span> books, etc.</em></li> </ul> <p>Plural noun ending in&nbsp;<strong>-s&nbsp;</strong>+&nbsp;<strong>‘&nbsp;</strong>(apostrophe)</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>The <span><strong>students’</strong></span> books, the <span><strong>boys’</strong></span> toys, the <span><strong>teachers’</strong></span> lounge, etc.</em></li> </ul> <p>Irregular plural noun (NOT ending in&nbsp;<strong>-s</strong>) +&nbsp;<strong>‘s</strong></p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>The <span><strong>children’s</strong></span> toys, <span><strong>men’s</strong></span> clothes, etc.</em></li> </ul> <p>When one thing belongs to two or more people, add&nbsp;<strong>‘s</strong> only after the last noun.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Paul and Katherine’s</strong></span> house, <span><strong>Anna and George’s</strong></span> car, etc.</em></li> </ul> <p>When we have two or more people, and each person has one thing, we add&nbsp;<strong>‘s&nbsp;</strong>after each person.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Anna’s and George’s</strong></span> cars</em> (Anna’s car and George’s car), <em><span><strong>Sally’s</strong></span> and <span><strong>Tim’s</strong></span> computers</em> (Sally’s computer and Tim’s computer).</li> </ul> <h3>Possessive&nbsp;<strong>of</strong></h3> <p>We use&nbsp;<strong>of</strong> and NOT&nbsp;<strong>‘s</strong> when we talk about things (and not people or pets).</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>the end <span><strong>of</strong></span> the street <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>the street<strong><span>‘s</span></strong> end <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>a picture <span><strong>of</strong></span> the eclipse <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>the eclipse<strong><span>‘s</span></strong> picture <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>the man <span><strong>of</strong></span> the match <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>the match<strong><span>‘s</span></strong> man <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h3>Compound nouns: the city centre</h3> <p>With nouns that are used together very often, we often use them together without&nbsp;<strong>of</strong> and without&nbsp;<strong>‘s</strong></p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>a <span><strong>school bus</strong></span></em></li> <li><em>the <strong><span>city centre</span></strong></em></li> <li><em>the <span><strong>car key</strong></span></em></li> </ul> <h3><strong>Whose</strong></h3> <h4>When do we use&nbsp;<strong>whose</strong>?</h4> <p>We use&nbsp;the question word&nbsp;<strong>whose</strong> to ask about possession. There are two possible forms:</p> <p><strong>whose</strong> + noun</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Whose</strong></span> car is this?</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Whose</strong></span> books are those?&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p><strong>whose</strong> without a noun</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Whose</strong></span>&nbsp;is this car?</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Whose</strong></span>&nbsp;are those books?&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>When we answer with the possessive&nbsp;<strong>‘s</strong>, we can also use&nbsp;<strong>‘s&nbsp;</strong>+ noun or&nbsp;<strong>‘s&nbsp;</strong>without a noun.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Whose</strong></span>&nbsp;is this car?</em></li> <li><em>It’s John<span><strong>‘s car</strong></span></em></li> <li><em>It’s John<span><strong>‘s</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>Whose</strong> vs <strong>who’s</strong></h4> <p><strong>Whose</strong> = possession (of who)</p> <p><strong>Who’s</strong> = who is</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Whose</strong></span> car is this?</em> <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Who’s</strong></span>&nbsp;car is this?</em> <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><strong><span>Who’s</span> </strong>that man in the lobby? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Whose </strong></span>that man in the lobby? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":438,"questions":[{"id":3800,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>George is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["the new boyfriend of my sister","my sisters' new boyfriend","my sister's new boyfriend"]}]},{"id":3801,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>All <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> are broken.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["the boys toys","the boys' toys","the toys of the boys"]}]},{"id":3802,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> are yellow. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["book's pages","books pages","pages of the book"]}]},{"id":3803,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Hellen's house","Hellens house","the house of Hellen"]}]},{"id":3804,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["my dogs collar","the collar of my dog","my dog's collar"]}]},{"id":3805,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You need to clean <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["the floor of the house","the floor's houses","the house's floor"]}]},{"id":3806,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>These are <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (= One car belongs to Tom and another car to Jenny.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["the cars of Tom and Jenny","Tom's and Jenny's cars","Tom and Jenny's cars"]}]},{"id":3807,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. (=Two people have one car.)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["the car of Tom and Jenny","Tom and Jenny's car","Tom's and Jenny's car"]}]},{"id":3808,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> helps me with my homework. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["The friend of my mum","My mum's friend","My mums' friend"]}]},{"id":3809,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I need to paint <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["the playroom of the children","the childrens' playroom","the children's playroom"]}]}]},{"id":439,"questions":[{"id":3810,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ picture is this?</div>","choices":[{"id":5793,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Whose</span>"},{"id":5794,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Who's</span>"},{"id":5795,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Whos</span>"}]},{"id":3811,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ is ill.</div>","choices":[{"id":5796,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>The father of Allan</span>"},{"id":5797,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Father's Edgar</span>"},{"id":5798,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Allan's father</span>"}]},{"id":3812,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ that man at the table?</div>","choices":[{"id":5799,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Whos</span>"},{"id":5800,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Who's</span>"},{"id":5801,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Whose</span>"}]},{"id":3813,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The shop is at _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":5802,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the end of the street</span>"},{"id":5803,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the street's end</span>"},{"id":5804,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the end's street</span>"}]},{"id":3814,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ is very expensive.</div>","choices":[{"id":5805,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>New car's Lucy</span>"},{"id":5806,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Lucy's new car</span>"},{"id":5807,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>The new car of Lucy</span>"}]},{"id":3815,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I love _____. </div>","choices":[{"id":5808,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the new book of Rowling</span>"},{"id":5809,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the new book's Rowling</span>"},{"id":5810,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Rowling's new book</span>"}]},{"id":3816,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ is this absurd idea?</div>","choices":[{"id":5811,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Who's</span>"},{"id":5812,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Whose</span>"},{"id":5813,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Whos'</span>"}]},{"id":3817,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ the person in the photo?</div>","choices":[{"id":5814,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Who's</span>"},{"id":5815,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Whos'</span>"},{"id":5816,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Whose</span>"}]},{"id":3818,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>In this school, 100% of _____ are recycled. All the students recycle their textbooks. </div>","choices":[{"id":5817,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the textbooks' students</span>"},{"id":5818,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the students' textbooks</span>"},{"id":5819,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the student's textbooks</span>"}]},{"id":3819,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ is next Sunday. </div>","choices":[{"id":5820,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Sheila and Mike's wedding</span>"},{"id":5821,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Sheila's and Mike's wedding</span>"},{"id":5822,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the wedding of Sheila and Mike</span>"}]}]},{"id":440,"questions":[{"id":3820,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The balls belong to the players. ⇒ They are <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3821,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The computer belongs to Sara. ⇒ It's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3823,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I hate the moustache that belongs to my brother. ⇒ I hate <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3824,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This car belongs to Sam and Pam. ⇒ It's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3822,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The money belongs to the workers. ⇒ It's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3825,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>These bikes belong to Mike and John (one bike to each person). ⇒ They are <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3826,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>These documents belong to the women. ⇒ They are <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3827,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This glass belongs to Mathew. ⇒ It's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3828,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This award belongs to the actresses. ⇒ It's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3829,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This suitcase belongs to Kate and David. ⇒ It's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}